1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,899
A signing call. A pinned dependency.

2
00:00:03,899 --> 00:00:07,903
A cipher list nobody has opened in years.

3
00:00:07,903 --> 00:00:12,150
A private key left inside a container image.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,337
One scan of the demonstration estate.

5
00:00:16,337 --> 00:00:21,363
Before anything else, it says the inventory is incomplete:

6
00:00:21,363 --> 00:00:26,843
one endpoint was refused. Then the numbers — 23 distinct assets,

7
00:00:26,843 --> 00:00:29,750
16 of them quantum-vulnerable.

8
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:35,835
Every asset gets a row, highest risk first.

9
00:00:35,835 --> 00:00:43,350
The top two are both RSA — and they need different replacements.

10
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:51,043
Three of the scan's RSA findings, side by side.

11
00:00:51,043 --> 00:00:59,867
A signing call — RSA-PSS padding — so the target is ML-DSA-65.

12
00:00:59,867 --> 00:01:10,319
A key wrapped with RSA-OAEP is key establishment, so a hybrid key exchange.

13
00:01:10,319 --> 00:01:17,012
A cipher list that permits RSA without saying

14
00:01:17,012 --> 00:01:21,950
what for gets no target at all.

15
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:27,181
Open the finding and the tool shows its working.

16
00:01:27,181 --> 00:01:30,709
Where the call is, and what it does.

17
00:01:30,709 --> 00:01:36,303
How strong the evidence is — a real call site, not a manifest.

18
00:01:36,303 --> 00:01:41,261
The exposure arithmetic under the operator's scenario.

19
00:01:41,261 --> 00:01:44,550
Only then, the target: ML-DSA-65.

20
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:50,932
The three answers become three workstreams: ML-DSA-65, the hybrid group,

21
00:01:50,932 --> 00:01:55,233
and the findings whose purpose must be resolved first

22
00:01:55,233 --> 00:02:00,514
— one workstream per replacement, which is how the work is staffed.

23
00:02:01,264 --> 00:02:04,940
It is as careful about what it did not see.

24
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:10,261
A key deleted by a later container layer is reported as historical

25
00:02:10,261 --> 00:02:13,508
— gone at runtime, still extractable.

26
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:18,114
A refused endpoint makes the scan PARTIAL, and says why.

27
00:02:18,864 --> 00:02:26,631
Open report, and the same scan becomes a document a director can read:

28
00:02:26,631 --> 00:02:32,714
the headline counts, then the assessment behind them.

29
00:02:33,464 --> 00:02:38,831
Validate, and the CycloneDX bill of materials is checked

30
00:02:38,831 --> 00:02:42,198
against the official JSON Schema

31
00:02:42,198 --> 00:02:46,314
— offline, at a pinned commit. It passes.

32
00:02:47,064 --> 00:02:50,426
Run it yourself: the demo,

33
00:02:50,426 --> 00:02:56,914
the 664 tests and the benchmark are all in the repository.
